---
import DocsLayout from '../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const params = [
  { group: 'Pose',  name: 'head_pitch, head_yaw, head_roll', range: 'deg, -25 to 25', desc: 'Head nod / turn / tilt offsets. Past about 8 deg the framing itself changes.' },
  { group: 'Pose',  name: 'move_x, move_y',                  range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Shift the face inside the crop.' },
  { group: 'Pose',  name: 'zoom',                            range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Face scale; negative shrinks.' },
  { group: 'Eyes',  name: 'eye_open',                        range: '0 to 1',         desc: 'Open the eyes further than captured. 0 leaves them alone.' },
  { group: 'Eyes',  name: 'wink',                            range: '0 to 1',         desc: 'Close one eye.' },
  { group: 'Eyes',  name: 'gaze_x, gaze_y',                  range: 'deg, -30 to 30 / -63 to 63', desc: 'Eyeball direction. Negative x is the performer left, negative y is down.' },
  { group: 'Brows', name: 'brow_raise',                      range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Brows up, or furrowed.' },
  { group: 'Mouth', name: 'lip_open',                        range: '0 to 1',         desc: 'Open the mouth further than captured.' },
  { group: 'Mouth', name: 'smile',                           range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Smile, or frown.' },
  { group: 'Mouth', name: 'pout, purse',                     range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Lip shapes.' },
  { group: 'Mouth', name: 'grin',                            range: '0 to 1',         desc: 'Wide grin.' },
  { group: 'Mouth', name: 'jaw_open',                        range: '-1 to 1',        desc: 'Jaw open, or clenched.' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Face Performance Edit - MHA Manager"
  description="Adjust a Mono take's facial performance with a marker timeline before it solves, using a locally installed face-edit backend."
  currentSlug="face-edit"
>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <h1 class="doc-title">Face Performance Edit</h1>
    <p class="doc-lead">
      A dead-eyed line or a missed smile normally means a reshoot. Right-click a
      <strong>Mono</strong> job, choose <strong>Edit Face Performance...</strong>, and drop markers on
      the take's timeline instead: the panel edits the take's RGB frames through a locally installed
      face-edit backend, then resets the job so the next batch re-solves the adjusted footage. The
      original frames are always kept.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Before you start</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      The plugin ships no model and no weights. Install a backend once, outside the plugin, and point
      the plugin at it. Until you do, the menu entry is greyed out and its tooltip says why.
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <pre><code>{'powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File Scripts\\Install-FaceEditBackend.ps1 -Root D:\\FaceEdit'}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="section-desc">
      The script clones the backend, builds its own Python 3.10 virtual environment, downloads its
      weights (about 1.5 GB), runs a self test, and writes a <code>backend.json</code> manifest. Paste
      the root it prints into <strong>Global Settings -&gt; External Tools -&gt; Face Edit Backend
      Root</strong>. Re-running the script is safe - every step is skipped when its result already
      exists. You need <code>git</code> and either Python 3.10 or <code>uv</code> on PATH, and an
      NVIDIA GPU with headroom beside the editor.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-warn">
      <strong>Check the backend's licence before commercial work.</strong> LivePortrait is the first
      supported backend: its own code is MIT, but the face-detection models it pulls in are licensed
      for non-commercial use only. The installer prints the notice; the plugin ships neither.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The panel</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Opening a session starts the backend - once per editor session, so the weights load once - and
      copies the take's frames aside. The header reports the take, frame count, fps, backend name, and
      state: Loading model, Loading footage, Ready, Rendering, or Error.
    </p>
    <div class="field-list">
      <div class="fe-row header">
        <span>Area</span>
        <span>What it does</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-row">
        <span><strong>Before / After</strong></span>
        <span>The scrubbed frame as captured, and the same frame previewed with the markers that reach it. The After pane stays blank on frames no marker touches - those frames are never rendered.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-row">
        <span><strong>Marker list</strong></span>
        <span>Add at Frame, Remove, Duplicate. Markers are keyframed adjustments, not a re-performance.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-row">
        <span><strong>Marker properties</strong></span>
        <span>Timing and parameter values for the selected marker. Rows the installed backend does not support are hidden.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-row">
        <span><strong>Direct</strong></span>
        <span>A plain-language note plus <strong>Send to Claude</strong>. See <a href="#directing">Directing in words</a>.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-row">
        <span><strong>Render / Cancel / Revert Footage</strong></span>
        <span>Render every touched frame over the take's footage, stop a render in progress, or restore the original frames.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="section-desc" style="margin-top:14px;">
      Markers and the note are stored per take, so reopening the panel picks up where you left off.
      The menu entry is greyed out while a batch is running, and on Stereo and Audio rows: editing one
      view of a stereo pair destroys the stereo consistency the depth solve depends on.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Markers</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      A marker has a frame, a ramp in, a hold, and a ramp out, all counted in frames. It is at full
      strength from <code>frame</code> to <code>frame + hold</code>, eases in over the frames before
      and out over the frames after, and is zero everywhere else. Overlapping markers sum, so a long
      mood marker plus short beats layer cleanly. Every value defaults to 0, meaning no change.
    </p>
    <div class="field-list">
      <div class="param-row header">
        <span>Group</span>
        <span>Parameter</span>
        <span>Range</span>
        <span>Meaning</span>
      </div>
      {params.map(p => (
        <div class="param-row">
          <span>{p.group}</span>
          <span><code>{p.name}</code></span>
          <span>{p.range}</span>
          <span>{p.desc}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="section-desc" style="margin-top:14px;">
      Values are model-neutral: degrees for pose and gaze, signed unit scalars for expressions. The
      backend maps them to its own ranges and declares which of them it supports. Subtle is 0.2-0.4,
      clear 0.5-0.7, big 0.8-1.0 - prefer smaller values over longer spans, because large pose and
      zoom values produce artifacts that the solver then faithfully tracks.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Render, and getting the take back</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Opening a session copies the take's frame folder to <code>&lt;folder&gt;_orig</code>, once. That
      pristine copy is the only thing the backend ever reads, so edits never chain: the marker list
      alone decides what the take looks like. Render then makes the live folder equal to "pristine plus
      the current markers" - touched frames are written over, frames an earlier render touched but the
      current markers do not are restored from the copy, and everything else is left byte-identical.
    </p>
    <p class="section-desc">
      The job is reset to <strong>Pending</strong> so the next <strong>Start Batch</strong> re-solves
      it, and the backup is recorded as an artifact on the job. File names and the folder do not
      change, so the take's Capture Data and its image sequence need no fixing up.
      <strong>Revert Footage to Original</strong> on the queue row restores the copy and resets the job
      again; it appears only on takes that have been edited.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      <strong>Ingested footage lives in a cache.</strong> Takes brought in through Live Link Hub /
      Capture Manager reference frames under the project's <code>Saved</code> cache, so the frames, the
      <code>_orig</code> copy, and the take itself are only as durable as that cache. Keep the raw
      footage you shot; a take is not an archive.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="directing">
    <h2 class="section-title">Directing in words</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Type the change you want - "subtle smile from 2s to 4s, glance left at 4.5s" - and press
      <strong>Send to Claude</strong>. That stores the note on the session; running
      <code>/mha-direct</code> in a Claude Code session next to the editor reads it, translates it into
      markers, and writes them back through
      <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/mcp-toolset">the MCP toolset</a>
      (<code>get_face_edit_session</code> and <code>set_face_edit_markers</code>). The panel refreshes
      on its own.
    </p>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Nothing renders on its own: markers arrive for you to scrub, preview, adjust, and render
      yourself. There is no render tool.
    </p>
  </section>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .doc-header { margin-bottom: 40px; }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 620px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .doc-lead strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .doc-section { margin-bottom: 48px; }

  .section-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .section-desc strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .field-list {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .fe-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.8fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 11px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .param-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.6fr 1.6fr 1.2fr 2.4fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 11px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .fe-row:last-child,
  .param-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .fe-row.header,
  .param-row.header {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .fe-row strong,
  .param-row strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .code-block {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .code-block pre { margin: 0; }

  .code-block code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #c9d1d9;
    line-height: 1.75;
    white-space: pre;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .callout {
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .callout-warn { background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 8%, transparent); border-color: #f0a500; }
  .callout-note { background: var(--bg-surface); border-color: var(--border); }
  .callout strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .fe-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .param-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
